<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ludovica Torelli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1500">1500</a>–<a href="/years/1569">1569</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ludovica Torelli was Countess of Guastalla and heiress of the Torelli family. In 1539 she sold Guastalla to Ferrante Gonzaga, a general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>, and devoted her fortune to religious works, founding in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> the Angelic Sisters of Saint Paul, a congregation linked to the Barnabites. She later established a college for girls in Milan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ludovica-torelli.jpg" alt="Ludovica Torelli" width="283" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ludovica_Torelli.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
